# Whole-struct subscope output — refused (PHASE5C-TUTORIAL §3)

A subscope output consumed as a whole struct value (here bound whole through
a `let`, rather than read one field at a time) is out of scope: the lowering
reads outputs per field over the back-link. A whole-struct read follows
design 1 (the StructType datatype) once both land.

```catala
declaration scope Kamer:
  input grondslag content integer
  output bedrag content integer

scope Kamer:
  definition bedrag equals grondslag * 2

declaration scope Aanslag:
  input grondslag content integer
  output heffing content integer

scope Aanslag:
  definition heffing equals
    let k equals (output of Kamer with { -- grondslag: grondslag }) in k.bedrag
```
